00:36:40.949 --> 00:36:43.416
Buddy, buddy, buddy, buddy!

245
00:36:43.660 --> 00:36:47.872
I've seen some bad-ass bush before, man,
but nothin' like this.

246
00:36:47.873 --> 00:36:52.126
I hear you.
This shit's somethin'.

247
00:36:52.219 --> 00:36:55.630
Makes Cambodia look like Kansas.

248
00:36:55.631 --> 00:36:59.501
Hey, qué pasa, amigo?
Little taste of home.

249
00:37:03.138 --> 00:37:07.308
You lose it here,
you're in a world of hurt.

250
00:37:15.025 --> 00:37:18.007
Come on, sweetheart.
Stop sandbaggin' it. Now, get up.

251
00:37:18.987 --> 00:37:22.005
Come on, get up.
Would you get up?

252
00:37:22.030 --> 00:37:23.545
Mierda!
*Shit

253
00:37:26.411 --> 00:37:29.030
Ni lo intentes.
*Don't even try

254
00:37:31.830 --> 00:37:35.239
Maybe you'd better
put her on a leash, agent man.

255
00:37:42.719 --> 00:37:46.405
Try it again... please.

256
00:38:37.691 --> 00:38:39.234
Callate!
*Shut up

257
00:38:50.037 --> 00:38:52.913
What's got Billy so spooked?

258
00:38:52.914 --> 00:38:57.585
Can't say, Major.
Been acting squirrelly all morning.

259
00:38:57.586 --> 00:39:01.540
That damn nose of his...
It's weird.

260
00:39:42.820 --> 00:39:44.649
What is it?

261
00:39:47.302 --> 00:39:49.026
Billy...

262
00:39:51.556 --> 00:39:54.539
What the hell is wrong with you?

263
00:39:58.063 --> 00:40:00.635
There's something in those trees.

264
00:40:37.310 --> 00:40:39.659
Do you see anything?

265
00:40:39.980 --> 00:40:42.182
Up there.

266
00:40:43.428 --> 00:40:45.045
Nothing.

267
00:40:46.027 --> 00:40:48.104
What do you think?

268
00:40:53.869 --> 00:40:56.425
I guess it's nothing, Major.

269
00:41:52.469 --> 00:41:54.011
Please!

270
00:41:54.012 --> 00:41:55.711
Please!

271
00:42:01.889 --> 00:42:03.628
Aaagh!

272
00:43:08.005 --> 00:43:11.675
Billy, break left.
Mac, right.

273
00:43:11.840 --> 00:43:13.854
What the...?

274
00:43:13.972 --> 00:43:16.362
- This isn't her blood.
- What the hell'd you do to him?

275
00:43:16.387 --> 00:43:19.781
Major... you'd better take a look at this.

276
00:43:19.806 --> 00:43:23.309
- Did you find Hawkins?
- I...

277
00:43:23.310 --> 00:43:25.765
I can't tell.

278
00:43:42.412 --> 00:43:45.164
What in God's name...?

279
00:43:45.165 --> 00:43:47.592
I think it's Hawkins.

280
00:43:48.835 --> 00:43:52.710
- Where the hell is his body?
- There's no sign of it.

281
00:43:54.215 --> 00:43:56.576
Ask her what happened.

282
00:44:00.805 --> 00:44:04.500
What happened?
What happened here?

283
00:44:04.525 --> 00:44:06.426
Qué fue lo que viste?
*What did you see?

284
00:44:06.451 --> 00:44:08.984
- Quién fue?  *Who was it?
- Yo no sé.    * I don't know.

285
00:44:09.009 --> 00:44:11.458


286
00:44:11.483 --> 00:44:14.209
- La selva se lo llevé.   * The jungle took him.
- Qué?                     * What?

287
00:44:14.234 --> 00:44:16.828
No estoy segura.  *I don't know.
No sé.                 * I'm not sure.

288
00:44:16.853 --> 00:44:20.675
She says the jungle...
It just came alive and took him.

289
00:44:20.700 --> 00:44:24.016
Bullshit!
That's not what she said!

290
00:44:24.456 --> 00:44:26.007
What she said doesn't
make any sense.

291
00:44:26.032 --> 00:44:27.748
Look. Those sappers have
followed us ever since...

292
00:44:27.749 --> 00:44:31.311
They'd been in front of us, man!
This woman is just ranting on...

293
00:44:31.336 --> 00:44:32.982
Hold it!

294
00:44:33.007 --> 00:44:37.091
Hold it!
Why didn't they take his radio or his weapon?

295
00:44:37.558 --> 00:44:39.837
Why didn't she escape?

296
00:44:42.806 --> 00:44:45.455
- Hopper.
- What?

297
00:44:47.114 --> 00:44:50.146
They did the same thing
 to Jim Hopper.

298
00:44:54.651 --> 00:44:57.369
I want Hawkins' body found.
Sweep pattern.

299
00:44:57.394 --> 00:45:00.364
Double back. 50 metres.
Let's go.

300
00:46:51.100 --> 00:46:56.314
Come on in, you fuckers.
Come on in.

301
00:46:56.339 --> 00:46:59.115
Old painless is waitin'.

302
00:47:27.813 --> 00:47:32.418
Contact!

303
00:47:35.191 --> 00:47:37.893
Motherfucker!

304
00:47:39.274 --> 00:47:42.201
Aaaah!

305
00:49:08.936 --> 00:49:11.062
- What happened?
- I saw it.

306
00:49:11.087 --> 00:49:13.579
- You saw what?
- I saw it.

307
00:49:30.885 --> 00:49:32.719
Blain...

308
00:49:32.835 --> 00:49:36.658
No powder burns, no shrapnel.

309
00:49:36.683 --> 00:49:39.855
The wound's all fused, cauterised.

310
00:49:39.880 --> 00:49:42.587
What the hell could have
done this to a man?

311
00:49:42.612 --> 00:49:44.196
Mac...

312
00:49:44.221 --> 00:49:46.365
Mac, look at me!

313
00:49:47.068 --> 00:49:48.388
Who did this?

314
00:49:48.413 --> 00:49:52.367
I don't know, goddamn it.
I saw something.

315
00:49:55.708 --> 00:49:58.662
Not a thing.
Not a fuckin' trace.

316
00:49:58.663 --> 00:50:02.608
No blood, no bodies.
We hit nothing.

317
00:50:09.515 --> 00:50:13.894
Dillon, better get on the radio.

318
00:50:14.929 --> 00:50:16.453
Mac...

319
00:50:17.475 --> 00:50:19.463
- Sergeant!
- Yes, sir.

320
00:50:19.488 --> 00:50:21.901
I want a defensive
position above that ridge,

321
00:50:21.926 --> 00:50:24.047
mined with everything we've got.

322
00:50:26.107 --> 00:50:28.537
Put him in his poncho.
Take him with us.

323
00:50:28.562 --> 00:50:30.236
I got him.

324
00:50:46.627 --> 00:50:48.389
Vémonos.
* Let's go.

325
00:51:34.371 --> 00:51:38.448
Major, I set up flares,
frags and claymores.

326
00:51:38.473 --> 00:51:42.005
Nothing's coming near this place
without tripping on somethin'.

327
00:51:42.394 --> 00:51:44.888
Thank you, Sergeant.

328
00:51:45.853 --> 00:51:47.629
Mac...

329
00:51:48.889 --> 00:51:51.756
He was a good soldier.

330
00:51:52.839 --> 00:51:54.970
He was, uh...

331
00:51:56.197 --> 00:51:58.245
my friend.

332
00:53:05.474 --> 00:53:07.431
Goodbye, bro.

333
00:54:08.287 --> 00:54:10.042
Aah!

334
00:54:14.335 --> 00:54:18.414
Blazer One,
I repeat, extraction necessary.

335
00:54:18.738 --> 00:54:21.404
Say again, Blazer One.
Say again.

336
00:54:21.429 --> 00:54:25.749
Request for extraction denied.
Area is still compromised.

337
00:54:25.774 --> 00:54:28.610
Proceed to sector 3,000
for prisoner extraction.

338
00:54:28.635 --> 00:54:31.702
Priority, out.
Next contact 0930.

339
00:54:31.727 --> 00:54:34.761
Roger, Blazer One.
1030 hours.

340
00:54:34.786 --> 00:54:36.953
Damn bastards.

341
00:54:36.978 --> 00:54:40.211
They say we're still in too far.
And they can't risk coming in after us.

342
00:54:40.236 --> 00:54:43.863
We're assets, Dillon.
Expendable assets.

343
00:54:43.864 --> 00:54:46.533
It comes with the job.
I can accept it.

344
00:54:46.534 --> 00:54:49.889
Bullshit.
You're just like the rest of us.

345
00:54:51.242 --> 00:54:54.979
A shitload of good a chopper's
gonna do us in here anyhow.

346
00:54:58.016 --> 00:55:00.815
Sergeant?
Sergeant!

347
00:55:00.840 --> 00:55:04.008
Sergeant!
Who hit us today?

348
00:55:04.427 --> 00:55:06.428
I don't know.

349
00:55:06.429 --> 00:55:09.210
I only saw one of them camouflaged.

350
00:55:10.149 --> 00:55:14.896
He was there.
Those eyes disappeared.

351
00:55:14.921 --> 00:55:16.923
What was that?

352
00:55:16.989 --> 00:55:21.235
Those eyes, they...
They disappeared.

353
00:55:21.777 --> 00:55:25.905
I know one thing, Major.
I drew and fired straight at it.

354
00:55:25.906 --> 00:55:30.380
Capped off 200 rounds
in the Minigun... Full pack.

355
00:55:30.405 --> 00:55:35.045
Nothing... nothing on this earth
could have lived.

356
00:55:35.564 --> 00:55:38.000
Not at that range.

357
00:55:40.488 --> 00:55:45.892
Mac, you take first watch,
then you get some rest.

358
00:55:46.035 --> 00:55:48.512
Ask her.
Ask her what she saw.

359
00:55:48.537 --> 00:55:50.805
Ask her what
happened to Hawkins.

360
00:55:51.777 --> 00:55:53.994
Go ahead.
Ask her.

361
00:55:54.204 --> 00:55:56.062
Qué pasé hoy?
*What happened today?

362
00:55:56.087 --> 00:55:58.879
- Qué fue lo que viste? - *What did you see?
-* I told you what I know. - Te dije lo que sé.

363
00:55:58.904 --> 00:56:01.575
Fue la selva la que se lo Ilevé.
* It was the jungle that took him.

364
00:56:01.600 --> 00:56:02.902
Qué més quieres que te diga?
*What do you want me to tell you?

365
00:56:02.927 --> 00:56:07.158
She says the same fuckin' thing.
The jungle, it came alive and took him.

366
00:56:08.057 --> 00:56:12.127
Billy... you know something.
 What is it?

367
00:56:12.853 --> 00:56:18.054
- I'm scared, Poncho.
- Bullshit. You ain't afraid of no man.

368
00:56:18.079 --> 00:56:21.148
There's something out there
waiting for us...

369
00:56:22.331 --> 00:56:24.738
and it ain't no man.

370
00:56:32.742 --> 00:56:35.284
We're all gonna die.

371
00:56:37.670 --> 00:56:39.462
The guy's losing it.
He's losing his cool.

372
00:56:39.463 --> 00:56:41.455
There's nothing but a couple of guys
running around out there.

373
00:56:41.480 --> 00:56:42.733
We got to take them down.

374
00:56:42.758 --> 00:56:45.719
You still don't understand,
Dillon, do you?

375
00:56:45.720 --> 00:56:52.167
Whatever it is out there,
it killed Hopper, and now it wants us.

376
00:56:57.315 --> 00:57:02.587
Here we are again, bro,
just you and me.

377
00:57:02.934 --> 00:57:06.353
Same kind of moon
and same kind of jungle.

378
00:57:06.394 --> 00:57:09.021
Real number 10 night, remember?

379
00:57:09.382 --> 00:57:14.432
Whole platoon, 32 men chopped into meat,
and we walk out, just you and me.

380
00:57:14.457 --> 00:57:18.619
Nobody else.
Right on top, bro.

381
00:57:19.420 --> 00:57:21.546
Not a scratch.
Not a fuckin' scratch.

382
00:57:21.547 --> 00:57:24.924
You know, whoever got you,
he'll come back again,

383
00:57:24.925 --> 00:57:28.394
and when he does,
I'm gonna cut your name right into him.

384
00:57:29.446 --> 00:57:33.437
I'm gonna cut your name into him.

385
00:57:52.203 --> 00:57:53.683
- What the hell is it?
- Mac!

386
00:57:57.127 --> 00:58:00.958
- This way! Over here!
- Mac, where are you?

387
00:58:02.004 --> 00:58:03.948
Mac!

388
00:58:04.131 --> 00:58:05.833
Aagh!

389
00:58:06.966 --> 00:58:08.550
Mac!

390
00:58:08.724 --> 00:58:10.034
Fuck you!

391
00:58:12.473 --> 00:58:15.449
Mac, where are you'?

392
00:58:15.810 --> 00:58:17.856
- Don't fuck with me.
- Mac?

393
00:58:19.438 --> 00:58:21.785
Mac!
Where are you?

394
00:58:23.609 --> 00:58:27.319
- Jesus.
- I got you, motherfucker.

395
00:58:27.344 --> 00:58:30.054
I killed you, you fuck.

396
00:58:30.079 --> 00:58:34.371
- Jesus! You killed a pig.
- What the...?

397
00:58:34.396 --> 00:58:36.329
Do you think you could have found
something bigger?

398
00:58:36.330 --> 00:58:39.608
Yeah. Fuck you, Poncho.
Fuck you!

399
00:58:40.648 --> 00:58:44.560
- Where's the girl?
- Ah, shit!

400
00:58:44.922 --> 00:58:47.750
Why the hell
wasn't anybody watching her?

401
00:58:51.529 --> 00:58:54.069
Why didn't she
try to get away?

402
00:58:54.094 --> 00:58:57.734
Look at her.
She's scared out of her mind.

403
00:58:57.785 --> 00:59:01.216
Major, you better take a look at this.

404
00:59:06.544 --> 00:59:09.137
Blain's body, it's gone.

405
00:59:09.775 --> 00:59:14.851
It came in through the tripwires.
Took it right out from under our noses.

406
00:59:28.482 --> 00:59:33.820
That boar had to set off the trip flare,
Major, cos there ain't no other tracks.

407
00:59:33.821 --> 00:59:38.408
How could anyone get through this
and carry out Blain without us knowing it?

408
00:59:38.409 --> 00:59:41.111
And why didn't he try
and kill one of us?

409
00:59:41.704 --> 00:59:44.252
He came in to get the body.

410
00:59:44.747 --> 00:59:49.343
- He's killing us one at a time.
- Like a hunter.

411
01:00:05.964 --> 01:00:08.480
He's using the trees.

412
01:00:19.199 --> 01:00:21.951
Yesterday, what did you see?

413
01:00:21.952 --> 01:00:25.237
- You're wasting your time.
- No more games.

414
01:00:28.417 --> 01:00:31.001
I don't know what it was.

415
01:00:32.046 --> 01:00:34.255
- It...
- Go on.

416
01:00:34.256 --> 01:00:37.717
It changed colours
like the chameleon.

417
01:00:37.718 --> 01:00:39.951
It uses the jungle.

418
01:00:40.123 --> 01:00:43.514
Are you sayin' that Blain and Hawkins
were killed by a fuckin' lizard?

419
01:00:43.515 --> 01:00:46.726
That's a bullshit psych job.
There's two or three men out there at the most.

420
01:00:46.727 --> 01:00:48.505
Fucking lizard!

421
01:00:51.468 --> 01:00:54.630
- What's your name?
- Anna.

422
01:00:59.657 --> 01:01:04.862
Anna, this thing is hunting us.
All of us.

423
01:01:05.645 --> 01:01:07.529
You know that.

424
01:01:10.219 --> 01:01:12.960
- What the hell do you think you are doing?
- Dillon, We need everyone.

425
01:01:12.961 --> 01:01:15.209
I'm taking her back.
We're out of here in 5 minutes.

426
01:01:15.234 --> 01:01:16.416
We're not going yet.

427
01:01:16.441 --> 01:01:18.381
Look. The rendezvous is 10
to 12 miles away from here.

428
01:01:18.406 --> 01:01:19.801
You think the chopper's
going to wait?

429
01:01:19.802 --> 01:01:24.999
Dillon, we make a stand now, or there
will be nobody left to go to the chopper.

430
01:01:25.024 --> 01:01:27.359
There is something else.

431
01:01:27.393 --> 01:01:31.307
When the big man was killed,
you must have wounded it.

432
01:01:31.332 --> 01:01:33.958
Its blood was on the leaves.

433
01:01:33.983 --> 01:01:37.395
If it bleeds, we can kill it.

434
01:02:04.799 --> 01:02:06.300
Look out.

435
01:02:26.612 --> 01:02:30.246
You really think this boy-scout
bullshit is gonna work.

436
01:02:30.247 --> 01:02:34.167
It can see our tripwires.
Maybe it can't see this.

437
01:02:34.168 --> 01:02:38.124
Instead of complaining,
maybe you should help.

438
01:03:36.897 --> 01:03:39.258
What makes you think
he's gonna come in through here?

439
01:03:39.283 --> 01:03:42.186
There are tripwires on
every tree for 50 yards.

440
01:03:42.211 --> 01:03:44.322
This is the only way in.

441
01:04:10.597 --> 01:04:13.349
When I was little,
we found a man.

442
01:04:13.350 --> 01:04:17.395
He looked like...
like, butchered.

443
01:04:17.396 --> 01:04:20.273
The old women in the village
crossed themselves

444
01:04:20.274 --> 01:04:23.764
and whispered crazy
things, said strange things,

445
01:04:23.789 --> 01:04:26.879
"El diablo, cazador de hombres."
* "The Devil, the hunter of men."

446
01:04:27.827 --> 01:04:31.135
Only in the hottest years this happens.

447
01:04:33.537 --> 01:04:36.511
And this year it grows hot.

448
01:04:37.749 --> 01:04:40.558
We begin finding our men.

449
01:04:40.752 --> 01:04:47.629
We found them sometimes without their
skin, and sometimes much, much worse.

450
01:04:51.346 --> 01:04:58.178
"El que hace trofeos de los hombres" means
"the demon who makes trophies of man."

451
01:05:16.914 --> 01:05:19.611
So, what are you gonna try next?
Cheese?

452
01:05:23.675 --> 01:05:26.394
Hey, Dutch.
Dutch!

453
01:06:33.654 --> 01:06:35.534
Holy shit!

454
01:06:48.249 --> 01:06:49.595
Look out!

455
01:06:49.620 --> 01:06:51.154
Aaagh!

456
01:07:11.541 --> 01:07:14.597
Got you, motherfucker!
I got you!

457
01:07:16.074 --> 01:07:18.367
I'm coming!

458
01:07:18.368 --> 01:07:19.452
Mac.

459
01:07:19.453 --> 01:07:22.335
Mac! Get Ramirez on his feet
and get to the chopper.

460
01:07:22.360 --> 01:07:23.098
Right.

461
01:07:23.099 --> 01:07:25.025
Hold it, Dutch.
I'm going after Mac.

462
01:07:25.050 --> 01:07:26.518
That's not your style, Dillon.

463
01:07:26.543 --> 01:07:30.379
Guess I picked up some bad habits from you.
Now get your people the hell outta here.

464
01:07:30.380 --> 01:07:32.603
You can't win this, Dillon.

465
01:07:33.133 --> 01:07:35.268
Maybe I can get even.

466
01:07:36.469 --> 01:07:38.162
Dillon.

467
01:07:42.976 --> 01:07:45.629
Just hold on to that damn chopper.

468
01:07:46.352 --> 01:07:47.967
Oh...

469
01:07:50.060 --> 01:07:51.887
Oh!

470
01:07:53.278 --> 01:07:55.905
He's busted up pretty bad, Major.

471
01:07:55.906 --> 01:07:58.284
I can make it. I can make it.

472
01:07:58.309 --> 01:08:00.681
- Get the radio. Forget the rest.
- Right.

473
01:08:00.994 --> 01:08:03.845
- Oh!
- Come on, Poncho.

474
01:08:04.145 --> 01:08:06.039
Aagh!

475
01:08:25.310 --> 01:08:28.604
♪ Long tall Sally, she's built sweet

476
01:08:28.605 --> 01:08:32.191
♪ She got everything that Uncle John need

477
01:08:32.192 --> 01:08:34.602
♪ Oh, baby

478
01:08:35.487 --> 01:08:36.904
♪ Baby

479
01:08:36.905 --> 01:08:39.615
♪ I'm gonna have me some fun tonight

480
01:08:39.616 --> 01:08:42.068
♪ I'm gonna have me some fun

481
01:08:42.160 --> 01:08:44.029
♪ I'm gonna have me some fun

482
01:08:44.037 --> 01:08:45.905
♪ I'm gonna have me some fun

483
01:08:45.997 --> 01:08:48.658
♪ I'm gonna have me some fun

484
01:09:09.521 --> 01:09:11.315
Turn around.

485
01:09:14.985 --> 01:09:16.891
Over here.

486
01:09:21.908 --> 01:09:23.576
Over here.

487
01:09:30.250 --> 01:09:31.852
Mac?

488
01:09:39.926 --> 01:09:42.796
Shh...

489
01:09:45.184 --> 01:09:49.989
Out there. 
Past them trees.

490
01:09:52.365 --> 01:09:54.152
You see it?

491
01:09:58.499 --> 01:10:01.879
I see you.

492
01:10:09.437 --> 01:10:11.519
I see it.

493
01:10:12.959 --> 01:10:14.813
